# The one place that states which earlier commit the upgrade proof starts from.
#
# bin/ci/build-older-zip.sh builds the release zip of this commit; the install smoke test
# installs that zip first, puts a product, its stock and an order in its tables, then installs
# the current zip over it. CI (reusable-package.yml) and bin/ci/smoke-suite.sh both build the
# earlier zip through that script, so this file is the only statement of the commit.
#
# This file is read as data, never run: it holds one line, SEOCART_UPGRADE_FROM= followed by
# the 40 lower-case hexadecimal digits of the commit, and nothing else but comments. The script
# refuses anything else, and a commit that is not an ancestor of the checkout.
#
# Choose a commit whose migrations are a strict prefix of today's: every migration the current
# code has and this commit lacks is then one the upgrade must record once. `sh
# bin/ci/install-smoke.sh` fails when the earlier zip holds a migration the current one does
# not. Move the commit forward only. Once the project has released a version, the pin becomes
# the commit of the previous release.

SEOCART_UPGRADE_FROM=01f428d9d970afdbd898f7ed018eea2a60dbf66c
